\section{Multiphysics Frameworks for Computational Homogenization}\label{30005839}

\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Shared notation.}$\mathbb N=\{1,2,\ldots\}$; the standard number fields have their usual meanings. All additional conventions are stated locally.


Computational homogenization couples microscopic cell problems to macroscopic effective fields. Thermoviscous dissipation couples heat flow with viscous mechanical losses; resonances are frequency-dependent responses of the microscale system. Multiphysics formulations couple mechanical fields to electromagnetic, thermal or chemical variables.

\paragraph{Catalogue wording retained for traceability.}
How should computational homogenization incorporate thermoviscous dissipation and relax strict resonance confinement; which frameworks best balance accuracy, efficiency, and flexibility; and can they extend to electro-magneto-mechanical, thermomechanical, and chemomechanical systems?

\paragraph{Scope and source qualification.}The source is a comparative modelling programme and supplies no universal accuracy functional or single optimal framework.

\subsection{Short English statement}
Develop homogenization frameworks that handle dissipation and broader resonances while balancing accuracy, efficiency and flexibility across coupled physical fields.

\subsection{Research attempt}
\paragraph{Model, date and investigated scope.}
OpenAI GPT-6 Astra (configured model \texttt{gpt-6-astra}), ultra reasoning; generated 11 October 2026. Derived the exact effective response and power balance of a damped resonator cell, exposing the loss of resonance in static closure.

\paragraph{Sources and literature check.}
Read the full supplied definition, catalogue wording, source qualifications and listed references for 30005839. No fresh status or novelty search was performed. The argument below proves its auxiliary statements directly and does not import an unverified external theorem.

\paragraph{A dissipative resonator cell.} Let \(u(t)\) be a macroscopic strain coordinate, \(q(t)\) an internal resonator, and
\[
 E=\tfrac12K u^2+g u q+\tfrac12kq^2+\tfrac12m\dot q^2,
 \quad m,k,K>0,\quad Kk>g^2.
\]
Take \(m\ddot q+\gamma\dot q+kq=-gu\), with \(\gamma>0\), and stress \(\sigma=Ku+gq\). Differentiation gives the exact power balance \(\dot E=\sigma\dot u-\gamma\dot q^2\). The condition \(Kk>g^2\) makes the stored quadratic form positive by completing the square.
\paragraph{Elimination retains frequency and loss.} For harmonic inputs proportional to \(e^{-i\omega t}\), eliminating \(q\) gives
\[
 \sigma(\omega)=\left(K-\frac{g^2}{k-m\omega^2-i\gamma\omega}\right)u(\omega).
\]
The imaginary part is negative for \(\omega>0\), consistent with the chosen Fourier convention and positive dissipation. Replacing the denominator by \(k\) produces the static modulus \(K-g^2/k\), but loses the resonance and frequency-dependent loss. In the time domain a purely instantaneous static law therefore cannot reproduce all harmonic responses of even this one-cell model.
\paragraph{Source comparison.} This explicit benchmark motivates internal variables or memory in a homogenized framework; it does not select a best framework without a norm, tolerance and cost metric. Heat production \(\gamma\dot q^2\) can be identified from the balance, but no heat equation, electromagnetic coupling, chemical transport or spatial homogenization error is derived. The first gap is a controlled elimination or retained-mode approximation for the source coupled cell problems, including accuracy across the relevant resonance range.

\paragraph{Verification and adversarial audit.}
Checked positivity by completing the square, harmonic sign convention, dissipation balance and the zero-frequency limit; no universal best-framework claim. Model self-audit only; no independent human mathematical verification. Applied contribution prompt A before drafting and B afterwards. Checked positivity by completing the square, harmonic sign convention, dissipation balance and the zero-frequency limit; no universal best-framework claim. First remaining gap: Obtain a controlled coupled-cell approximation across the source resonance range with explicit error and computational cost. The inherited source status is preserved; original-target completion remains zero.

Coordinator checked the resonator power balance, positive stored quadratic form and complex effective-modulus sign. This additional check was model-assisted, not independent human verification.

\paragraph{Tools, process and contributions.}
Python 3 and local file tools used to read definitions and serialize manuscripts. Calculations are symbolic reasoning; no numerical experiment or theorem prover. Contribution prompt A was followed by prompt B. GPT-6 Astra with ultra reasoning drafted the research and performed its stated self-audit; any additional coordinator contribution is identified in the verification and audit. A GPT-6-based Codex coordinator assembled the manuscript and checked repository integration; its exact variant and reasoning configuration were not exposed. No human mathematical contribution, independent human proof check or formal proof certification is supplied. Complete derivations and the consulted source references are included here; private reasoning transcripts are not published.

\paragraph{Final status and first remaining gap.}
\textbf{UNRESOLVED}. Obtain a controlled coupled-cell approximation across the source resonance range with explicit error and computational cost.

